>
>> On Tuesday, April 22, 2014 09:12:38 neit wrote:
>> > coi rodo
>> >
>> > A good example that I'm trying to wrap my brain around is the following:
>> > Suppose I want to say, "Who wants my dog?"  bau la lojban - .i ma djica
>> lo
>> > nu ____ ponse lo mi gerku
>> >
>> > I want a sumka'i in the ____ to refer to the "ma" in the main bridi.
>>  How
>> > can I do that?  Can I use the reflexive sumka'i vo'a?  (.i ma djica lo
>> nu
>> > vo'a ponse lo mi gerku)?  Or do those reflexive sumka'i only refer to
>> their
>> > native bridi, or can they "reach-out" and refer to the main bridi of
>> which
>> > they are a part?
>>
>> I'd use "ce'u", since it's in a nu-clause.
>>
>> Pierre
>> --
>> ve ka'a ro klaji la .romas. se jmaji
